  m_Name: dragonfly
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WordInfo
  words:
  - dragonfly
  - dragonflies
  info: 'A dragonfly is a winged insect in the order Odonata. Dragonflies have long
    bodies, two pairs of strong, transparent wings, and eyes that give them nearly
    360-degree vision. They are apex predators, using exceptional flight agility
    and motion camouflage to ambush their prey. Dragonflies are among the most successful
    predators on Earth, with hunting studies reporting a kill rate of approximately
    97%. They are also one of the oldest groups of insects, with ancestors of modern
    dragonflies dating back around 300 million years, though the modern forms seen
    today appeared roughly 200 million years ago.


    Sources:

    https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonfly

    https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/dragonflies-the-ultimate-hunters.html'
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 224f94353ed36c34eabae0ac08401076, type: 3}
